-- ============================================================================
-- carbon ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Carbon & Energy Efficiency, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE INVENTORY. Combustion CO2 is carbon counted atom by
-- atom, never an empirical factor; a flare is one line of the inventory and
-- its destruction efficiency is an input nobody may leave blank; carbon that
-- escapes is counted as methane; a GWP set carries its report and its
-- horizon; a factor is a record with a source and a version; an inventory can
-- be computed and still not be reportable; an intensity names its boundary.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. A missing value stays missing. A blank
-- destruction efficiency is refused rather than read as 100 percent, a line
-- with no factor is blocked and named, and an undeclared GWP set blocks every
-- methane line.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A flare read as 100 percent destruction is
-- the best case, and it drops the methane line from the inventory entirely.
--
-- HELD, taught as limits and never graded: which IPCC report to file on (H1),
-- the typical methane heating value pair (H2), escaped carbon counted as
-- methane (H3), combustion N2O not computed (H4). The capstone grades six
-- figures in tonnes, each to two decimals, at a tolerance of 0.01 t, on the
-- IPCC AR6 100-year set with fossil methane stated in the prompt.
-- ============================================================================

values ('carbon', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-an-inventory-counts","title":"What an Inventory Counts","lesson_keys":["l01-two-apps-and-one-ledger","l02-scope-1-and-scope-2","l03-missing-stays-missing","l04-what-the-engines-will-not-ship"]},{"key":"m02-carbon-in-co2-out","title":"Carbon In, CO2 Out","lesson_keys":["l01-the-atom-balance","l02-molar-masses-from-atomic-weights","l03-carbon-per-kilomole-of-fuel","l04-a-fired-heaters-co2","l05-what-the-atom-balance-refuses"]},{"key":"m03-the-flare-as-an-inventory-line","title":"The Flare as an Inventory Line","lesson_keys":["l01-destruction-efficiency-is-an-input","l02-a-blank-box-is-missing","l03-what-escapes-is-counted-as-methane","l04-one-flare-at-five-efficiencies"]},{"key":"m04-global-warming-potentials","title":"Global Warming Potentials","lesson_keys":["l01-a-set-carries-its-report","l02-ar5-and-ar6","l03-fossil-and-non-fossil-methane","l04-one-inventory-on-four-sets","l05-which-set-to-file-on"]},{"key":"m05-lines-factors-and-provenance","title":"Lines, Factors and Provenance","lesson_keys":["l01-a-factor-is-a-record","l02-blocked-and-unsourced-lines","l03-the-scope-totals","l04-computed-and-reportable","l05-intensity-and-its-boundary"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-igbogene-inventory-end-to-end","l02-what-is-held-in-the-inventory","l03-what-the-next-tier-changes"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
